kind of testing. But it basically follows the same sensory changes that you would use. It's a field called psychophysics that is used in vision and hearing as well. It's just done with odorants instead of letters or sounds. Most patient sense of smell does seem to come back, I understand, but for those who have long-lasting effects, is there hope or there treatments that you can use to help people regain their sense of smell? And can you train yourself to smell again? There is some hope. It turns out that at least with COVID, most people do recover their sense of smell. Sometimes even in a week or two following the initial other symptoms or their positive diagnosis. Some take up to two to three to three.

